  "problem_statement": "NumberUtils.min / max varargs lose the sign of zero\n\nRepro: `NumberUtils.max(-0.0d, 0.0d)` returns `-0.0` (so `1 / result` is `-Infinity`); `NumberUtils.min(0.0d, -0.0d)` returns `0.0`. The `float` overloads behave the same way.\n\nExpected: the same results as `Math.max` / `Math.min`, the three-argument `NumberUtils.min`/`max` overloads and `IEEE754rUtils`, which return `0.0` for max and `-0.0` for min here. Existing `NaN` handling should stay the same.",
  "fail_to_pass": [
    "org.apache.commons.lang3.math.NumberUtilsTest::testMinMaxSignedZero"
  ],
